{
  "recommendations": {
    "W-001": {
      "fix": "The search endpoint /search reflects user input without proper output encoding. Implement context-aware escaping in the template (e.g., HTML encode) and add a Content Security Policy with 'unsafe-inline' removed to mitigate impact.",
      "effort": "low"
    },
    "W-002": {
      "fix": "The product listing endpoint /rest/products builds SQL queries with unsanitized parameters. Replace dynamic string concatenation with parameterized queries using an ORM or prepared statements, and enforce least-privilege database accounts.",
      "effort": "medium"
    },
    "W-003": {
      "fix": "The login endpoint /rest/user/login may be vulnerable to SQL injection. Use parameterized authentication queries, implement rate limiting and account lockout, and ensure passwords are hashed with strong algorithms.",
      "effort": "medium"
    },
    "W-004": {
      "fix": "/api/Users lacks proper authentication checks. Enforce authentication and authorization middleware, and restrict access to sensitive user fields via response filtering or DTOs.",
      "effort": "medium"
    },
    "W-005": {
      "fix": "The feedback submission /api/Feedbacks does not sanitize or encode stored content. Validate input on the server, encode output when rendering, and implement a CSP with 'unsafe-inline' disabled.",
      "effort": "medium"
    },
    "W-006": {
      "fix": "The basket items endpoint /api/BasketItems allows access by object reference without ownership checks. Implement authorization checks to ensure users can only access their own basket items, and use unpredictable IDs.",
      "effort": "medium"
    },
    "W-007": {
      "fix": "The addresses endpoint /api/Addresss is vulnerable to IDOR, allowing access to other users' addresses. Implement object-level authorization by verifying the authenticated user owns the address before returning data.",
      "effort": "medium"
    },
    "W-008": {
      "fix": "The cards endpoint /api/Cards allows IDOR, permitting access to other users' payment cards. Enforce authorization to restrict card data access to the owner, and consider tokenization to avoid storing sensitive data.",
      "effort": "medium"
    },
    "W-009": {
      "fix": "The admin configuration endpoint /rest/admin/application-configuration is accessible without proper authorization. Restrict access to admin roles and ensure the endpoint is not exposed publicly; also remove any sensitive data from the response.",
      "effort": "low"
    },
    "W-010": {
      "fix": "The security questions endpoint /api/SecurityQuestions allows enumeration. Implement rate limiting and access controls, and do not return the actual questions without authentication; consider generic questions.",
      "effort": "low"
    },
    "W-011": {
      "fix": "The password reset endpoint /rest/user/reset-password was not tested but is likely susceptible to abuse. Implement a secure token-based reset flow with expiry, and enforce rate limiting and CAPTCHA to prevent automated attacks.",
      "effort": "high"
    },
    "W-012": {
      "fix": "The file upload endpoint /file-upload is untested but may allow insecure file types. Validate file extensions, MIME types, and content, store files in a non-executable location, and scan for malware.",
      "effort": "medium"
    },
    "W-013": {
      "fix": "The order history endpoint /rest/order-history is untested but likely permits IDOR. Implement ownership checks to ensure users can only view their own orders, and use indirect object references.",
      "effort": "medium"
    },
    "W-014": {
      "fix": "The continue code endpoint /rest/continue-code/apply appears to lack authentication. Require authentication and authorization, and validate that the continue code belongs to the authenticated user; also implement rate limiting.",
      "effort": "high"
    },
    "W-015": {
      "fix": "The whoami endpoint /rest/user/whoami may expose sensitive data. Restrict the response to the minimum necessary fields, and ensure the endpoint is protected by authentication and not returning internal data.",
      "effort": "low"
    }
  },
  "narrative": "The application has a high-risk posture with many unproven critical vulnerabilities, especially SQL injection and authentication bypass, which could lead to full data compromise. Only a few low-severity issues are confirmed, so the unproven findings should be treated as hypotheses requiring further verification. The immediate priority is to validate and remediate the critical unproven findings (SQLi, auth bypass) through manual testing and code review, while confirming the confirmed low-risk issues can be fixed quickly. Because most findings are unproven, confidence in the overall risk level is moderate; there may be additional undetected issues. The CISO should allocate resources for a focused retest and implement security controls to prevent these classes of vulnerabilities across the board."
}

